          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Pierre Curie</strong><br>\nPierre Curie was born in Paris, France, on May 15, 1859. From a young age, he showed a strong interest in science and mathematics. His father, a physician, provided him with a solid education at home. This early academic environment set the stage for his later achievements in the field of physics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Research</strong><br>\nPierre Curie excelled in his studies and demonstrated a particular talent for physics. After completing his higher education, he began working as a laboratory instructor while conducting his own research. His early work focused on crystallography and the effects of temperature on magnetism.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Discoveries in Magnetism</strong><br>\nCurie's significant contributions to physics include his work on magnetism. He discovered that magnetic properties of materials change at a certain temperature, which is now known as the Curie point. This finding was crucial for developing the field of electromagnetism and advancing modern technology.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
